  "evidence": "- TEXT_G: Proportionality and merit emphasis via a single 31% flat income tax (merging Income Tax and NI), phasing out Employers’ NI, replacing 70+ benefits with a flat Basic Cash Benefit and instituting Workfare; strong authority/loyalty stances with “life means life,” a three-strikes policy, major defence expansion, support for the monarchy and Church of England, loyalty undertakings for residents, and leaving the EU; some care commitments like no frontline NHS cuts and health vouchers.\n- TEXT_F: Equality/care emphasis through protecting NHS budgets, creating a National Care Service, expanding childcare and minimum wage rises; progressive taxation (50p top rate, bank bonus tax, NI rise); moderate authority via maintaining police numbers and use of CCTV/DNA; pro‑EU leadership stance.",
